// B4 (2026-09-30): A THREAD OP INSIDE A SPAWNED BRANCH. `current_id()` is an
// op of the schedule's own effect, answered by the `parallel_compose`
// installed at the fanout's frame — so a branch asking which instance it
// runs on reaches the handler that spawned it. Boot 6f2ce437 faulted at the
// chain's end (exit 134, `ev_declaring_node` at 0xffffffff): the task
// record carried the spawn ARM's world, which by the deep-handler law
// excludes the schedule handler itself, so the branch could answer every
// handler outside the schedule and none of the schedule's own ops. The
// record carries the world of the PERFORM now.
// Expected exit: 14.
fn main() = match ((current_id()) >< (current_id())) ~> parallel_compose {
  (a, b) => if a > 0 && b > 0 { 14 } else { 1 },
}
